kmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@hillview5750 Saw your concerns about your daughter. ❤️ Neuralink  promising brain-computer interface technology, is a proven treatment for cerebral palsy hemiplegia. Please inbox me for more information and to put your daughter on the list 😊", "url": "https://x.com/sheMaryBurke/status/2114695606430228800"}, {"author_id": "1162343720232071168", "created_at": "2026-10-27T17:10:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115129019507396909"], "id": "2115129019507396909", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 23, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "The Time I Ran Into A Brain Computer Interface Patient In DayZ \n#dayz #gaming #pc #xbox #playstation #switch\nhttps://t.co/bi6FQpMIET via @YouTube", "url": "https://x.com/forgamessake/status/2115129019507396909"}, {"author_id": "2292534031", "created_at": "2026-10-26T11:52:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114686706482077850"], "id": "2114686706482077850", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 22, "impression_count": 3341, "like_count": 69, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "Shen et al. found that one third of clinically unresponsive patients with acute brain injury were able to control a brain-computer interface, suggesting communication may be possible despite a lack of behavioural responses. https://t.co/QuG8K03EEa https://t.co/f7epgMNl8g", "url": "https://x.com/Brain1878/status/2114686706482077850"}, {"author_id": "1961430593905774593", "created_at": "2026-10-26T20:54:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114822902461944310"], "id": "2114822902461944310", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 25, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "1/ They can't move. Can't blink on command. Can't speak. But their brain is awake — and this week, it answered. Columbia researchers built a brain-computer interface that lets unresponsive ICU patients communicate with thought alone. 🧵 https://t.co/aAhRU40ULZ", "url": "https://x.com/hew17w/status/2114822902461944310"}, {"author_id": "1305558731690631169", "created_at": "2026-10-27T17:03:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115127341219205350"], "id": "2115127341219205350", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Research news: a UCSF team's brain-computer interface let people with paralysis express speech and gestures at once through a virtual avatar. It's early-stage, but a step toward more natural communication. Summary from NIH: https://t.co/gyYhLqwtJ8", "url": "https://x.com/everydayability/status/2115127341219205350"}, {"author_id": "1638823713129873411", "created_at": "2026-10-27T11:58:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115050384842789000"], "id": "2115050384842789000", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A new milestone for #brain-computer interface research. \n\n@paradromics received #FDA approval to expand Connexus clinical study recruitment nationwide—potentially widening access to participation.\n\n👉 https://t.co/Z7QVf5fpNd\n\n#Neurotech #Neurotechnology #MedTech #ClinicalResearch https://t.co/EnsnBsssiH", "url": "https://x.com/am_hhm/status/2115050384842789000"}, {"author_id": "2802592903", "created_at": "2026-10-27T04:10:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114932758900289806"], "id": "2114932758900289806", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 88, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "i suffered until i got my brain-computer interface. it’s a device that can stimulate/record the brain's neural activity, controlling/modulating the functions and consciousness. it cured my mental illness and treated the uremia symptoms from my kidney failure.", "url": "https://x.com/brianpricejr/status/2114932758900289806"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "1249537969507037184", "name": "The Innovation: a Cell Press partner journal", "username": "The_InnovationJ"}, {"id": "80553919", "name": "iscab.saptocondro", "username": "saptocondro"}, {"id": "329402736", "name": "Will", "username": "medtechmd"}, {"id": "555031989", "name": "Ronald van Loon", "username": "Ronald_vanLoon"}, {"id": "1981362026812252161", "name": "DFM WORLD", "username": "dfmword"}, {"id": "1428708421964951556", "name": "HashDork", "username": "HashDork"}, {"id": "16840604", "name": "umbccsee", "username": "umbccsee"}, {"id": "1489333057031184387", "name": "⅄ʞu0ɥ 🦇 🔋 ☠🤝", "username": "h0nkY_swiss"}, {"id": "704115137116942336", "name": "blackorbird", "username": "blackorbird"}, {"id": "174981490", "name": "Jason Choi", "username": "mrjasonchoi"}, {"id": "908518769680564224", "name": "Conventus Tech", "username": "ConventusCyber"}, {"id": "763730717079642112", "name": "Nicholas Morris", "username": "namorrismd"}, {"id": "1677992691597017088", "name": "ATM", "username": "FORECAST_ONE"}, {"id": "1260834241371348994", "name": "Stock Catcher", "username": "MorningMadness4"}, {"id": "1614362310860017664", "name": "🏝️", "username": "dbr_islands"}, {"id": "407766714", "name": "Nat Rev Neurology", "username": "NatRevNeurol"}, {"id": "1678286417837916160", "name": "BrandlyMorton🇺🇸", "username": "BrandlyMo"}, {"id": "2085777715790229504", "name": "Dr Mary Burke| TSLA", "username": "sheMaryBurke"}, {"id": "1162343720232071168", "name": "ForGamesSake", "username": "forgamessake"}, {"id": "2292534031", "name": "Brain", "username": "Brain1878"}, {"id": "1961430593905774593", "name": "Hew", "username": "hew17w"}, {"id": "1305558731690631169", "name": "Everyday Abilities Foundation", "username": "everydayability"}, {"id": "1638823713129873411", "name": "AmericanHHM", "username": "am_hhm"}, {"id"